A||||7||007DOUG||My recent TX trip, and a little philosphopy (long)||||1||
Z||000000||007DOUG||05-14-2001||12:18 AM||||Last weekend, I made a quick 3,000 mile round trip to San Antonio and Houston Texas to "rescue" two Indy fieros.<P>Neither Indy ran. I was expecting the worst for both, but NEVER expected what I got. Here's the story.<P>Indy #1 wasn't even an Indy. Why did I think it was an Indy?? I asked the owner if.....<P>The fiero was an 84???...YES. Actually its an 85 <P>The fiero had red interior???...YES. The doorpanels were red (red spray paint), the carpet was red. Also found the fiero to have a red crushed velour headliner (lowrider special).<P>Is the fiero white???....No, its green. BUT it was white at one time (and black, and red).<P>I still bought the 85 coupe. The owner asked me "Senor Doug, is this the fiero". I'm standing there thinking to myself...."1500 miles, 23 hours, and hundreds of dollars in fuel for a fiero I could buy around the corner from my house". But as I looked at his kids with no shoes, his pregnant wife, his broken truck, and his small home.....I smiled and said "yes, its exactly what I'm looking for".<P>Indy #2, I never even got to see. I made arrangements with the owner to pick-up the fiero, but he "forgot". After several attempts, I headed home. 11 hours later while driving through Alabama, I got a call from him. He was home now, and I could pick-up the car. I wasn't turning around.<P>As if my trip couldn't get any worse, my trailer bearings went bad 2 hours from home. I had to leave the fiero at a truckstop in Columbus, OH for a week. I had to replace the entire axle.<P>I've traveled many times for fieros, but never had an experience like this. What have I learned from this trip.......ask for pictures before departing.<P>I want to take a moment to thank god. I have the ability, opportunity, health, knowledge, and resources to make a trip like this. A trip for stupid cars.<P>Fieros are ONLY cars, they are not what's important in my life. If my garage would burn tonight, or I wreck my fiero in the morning (or even scratched) It wouldn't REALLY matter. I know where to draw the line between fun, and obsession. <P>So, without further delay, here's my 85 green Indy: <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/txindy1_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>86 GT red (twins) <BR>86 GT Yellow ASAP<BR>86 GT w/4:10 tranny<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>88 Formula 5 speed<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||RobertVol||05-14-2001||12:27 AM||||Sorry to hear Doug!<P>But At least you got it in perspective. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>BTW check to INDY in the mall.<P><BR>Glad to see ya back on the Forum. Havnt seen ya in a while ||||reg||1
